outh cleft.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Do not draw eyelashes or iris detail yet; focus on the planar masses and eye-to-eye spacing (one eye-width apart).",recommendedPencilGrade:"HB",companionTool:"loomis"},{stepNumber:6,title:"Terminator Line & Shadow Separation",action:`Identify the main light direction (${s.lightSourceDirection}). Map the sharp terminator boundary separating the lit side of the face from shadow areas.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Squint through your eyelashes at your reference to blur details and spot the big shape of the shadow pattern.",recommendedPencilGrade:"HB",companionTool:"shading"},{stepNumber:7,title:"Unified Form Shadow Tone",action:`Fill all core shadow zones (${s.coreShadows.slice(0,2).join(", ")}) and cast shadows with an even, unbroken tone.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Hatch in parallel diagonal strokes with a flat lead bevel. Do not blend or smudge with fingers.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2B",companionTool:"shading"},{stepNumber:8,title:"Midtones, Occlusion Accents & Highlights",action:`Model subtle halftones inside the light mass. Accent dark occlusion crevices (${s.castShadows[0]??"under chin"}) and lift bright highlights (${s.highlightRegions[0]??"forehead"}) with a kneaded eraser.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Rest your hand on a clean slip-sheet of paper to prevent dragging graphite across finished light tones.",recommendedPencilGrade:"4B",companionTool:"shading"}];case"figure":return[{stepNumber:1,title:"60-Second Dynamic Line of Action",action:"Capture the sweeping gravitational curve from the base of the skull down through the spine and primary weight-bearing foot.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Hold your pencil with an overhand grip. Sweep with broad shoulder motion in a continuous fluid stroke.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2H",companionTool:"measurement"},{stepNumber:2,title:"8-Head Proportional Height Division",action:"Mark 8 equal vertical divisions. Anchor the pubic arch at the 4-head halfway mark, and kneecaps at unit 6.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Use a scrap paper tick-strip to verify all 8 units are identical before drawing anatomical volumes.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2H",companionTool:"grid"},{stepNumber:3,title:"Contrapposto Torso Tilt & Volumes",action:"Note the opposing angles between shoulder girdle and pelvic bowl. Construct the ribcage egg and pelvic basin with interlocking centerlines.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Draw the pinch on the weight-bearing side with sharp curves, and the stretched flank with an elongated curve.",recommendedPencilGrade:"H",companionTool:"anatomy"},{stepNumber:4,title:"Limb Cylinders & Joint Nesting",action:"Wrap tapering volumetric cylinders around limb axes. Ensure joints interlock with high outer curves opposing low inner curves.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Draw through hidden lines to confirm limbs connect solidly into the pelvic and shoulder sockets.",recommendedPencilGrade:"HB",companionTool:"anatomy"},{stepNumber:5,title:"Contour Hierarchy & Overlap",action:"Refine anatomical silhouettes. Darken contours where foreground masses overlap background forms (thigh overlapping knee).",physicalPaperGuidance:"Vary line weight: thicker at contact points and crevices, delicate on top-lit surfaces.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2B",companionTool:"bargue"},{stepNumber:6,title:"Tonal Massing & Directional Lighting",action:`Establish the terminator along the body's major muscle planes following the light direction (${s.lightSourceDirection}). Shade shadow masses uniformly.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Keep shadows unified and dark; avoid overworking internal highlights inside the shadow side.",recommendedPencilGrade:"4B",companionTool:"shading"}];default:return[{stepNumber:1,title:"Bounding Envelope & Benchmark Unit",action:`Observe the overall composition (${n.subjectPlacement}). Establish a base measuring unit and mark the outer envelope bounding box.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Extend arm fully with locked elbow when sighting. Transfer relative proportional units with tick marks.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2H",companionTool:"measurement"},{stepNumber:2,title:"Horizon Line & Vanishing Points",action:`Locate eye level (horizon). Trace converging edges (${o.perspectiveDirection??"Linear perspective convergence"}) toward left and right vanishing points.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Use a long plastic ruler to verify that receding parallel lines converge toward common points on the horizon.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2H",companionTool:"perspective"},{stepNumber:3,title:"Geometric Wireframe Construction",action:`Construct forms using basic 3D volumes (${o.basicGeometricConstruction.slice(0,2).join(", ")}). Draw through all transparent hidden edges.`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Keep wireframe lines light and crisp. Ensure ellipses align perpendicular to their cylinder core axes.",recommendedPencilGrade:"H",companionTool:"perspective"},{stepNumber:4,title:"Plumb Lines & Negative Space Check",action:"Drop vertical plumb lines through key landmarks. Compare the negative shapes formed between objects to verify spacing.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Hold your pencil vertically against the reference and check which corners align with the plumb line.",recommendedPencilGrade:"HB",companionTool:"grid"},{stepNumber:5,title:"Terminator & Cast Shadow Mapping",action:`Trace the core shadow terminator and project cast shadow boundaries (${s.castShadows[0]??"onto ground plane"}) based on the light source (${s.lightSourceDirection}).`,physicalPaperGuidance:"Ensure cast shadows are sharpest nearest to the contact point and softer further away.",recommendedPencilGrade:"2B",companionTool:"shading"},{stepNumber:6,title:"5-Step Value Modeling & Final Accents",action:"Shade from darkest darks to lightest midtones. Add deep ambient occlusion at contact points and lift specular highlights.",physicalPaperGuidance:"Keep Box 1 white paper untouched for the brightest specular highlights.",recommendedPencilGrade:"4B",companionTool:"shading"}]}}},1723,[]);
